<page type="text"><layout>One page of text in two parallel columns of verse, left column longer, right column shorter beside it; running head at the top centre with page number at the top right. No margin notes.; One column of verse, centred, in italic; below it at left a catchword line "Collegiorum jocus," and at the foot the signature "rrrr 2" with the catchword "Præ-" at right.</layout><page_number>683</page_number><running_head>BABYLONIS MAGNÆ.</running_head><bottom_margin><catchword>Præ-</catchword><signature>rrrr 2</signature></bottom_margin><main_text><l><i>In seculo passatum.</i></l>
    <l><i>Emergit insolentia,</i></l>
    <l><i>Recedit conscientia,</i></l>
    <l><i>Communiter à Clero:</i></l>
    <l><i>Quæ, qualis, quanta furia</i></l>
    <l><i>Committitur in Curia?</i></l>
    <l><i>De Curtisanis quæro.</i></l>
    <l><i>Nam illi sciunt practicam</i></l>
    <l><i>De Simone trussaticam,</i></l>
    <l><i>Scripturas &amp; Calendas:</i></l>
    <l><i>Quas ille mille artifex,</i></l>
    <l><i>Diabolus, eorum rex</i></l>
    <l><i>Invenit exercendas:</i></l>
    <l><i>Ut pauperes abjiciant,</i></l>
    <l><i>Et divites alliciant,</i></l>
    <l><i>In modis &amp; in formis..</i></l>
    <l><i>Quid aliud per atria,</i></l>
    <l><i>Quàm patens idolatria,</i></l>
    <l><i>Et Clericus enormis.</i></l>
    <l><i>Non psallitur Davidicè,</i></l>
    <l><i>Sed prorsùs hypocriticè,</i></l>
    <l><i>De beneficiatis:</i></l>
    <l><i>Qui qualiter &amp; quomodo</i></l>
    <l><i>Servire solent Domino,</i></l>
    <l><i>Jam dicebatur satis.</i></l>
    <l><i>Nunc de eorum vestibus,</i></l>
    <l><i>Et moribus &amp; gestibus,</i></l>
    <l><i>Ad modicum tractabo:</i></l>
    <l><i>In quibus fatualiter,</i></l>
    <l><i>Et merè laicaliter</i></l>
    <l><i>Incedunt, increpabo.</i></l>
    <l><i>Canonici cum cæteris</i></l>
    <l><i>Collegiatis sociis,</i></l>
    <l><i>Mundaniter imbuti,</i></l>
    <l><i>In varis &amp; sérico</i></l>
    <l><i>Vestiti vadunt Jericho,</i></l>
    <l><i>Mollissimis induti.</i></l>
    <l><i>Ne quid eorum corpora</i></l>
    <l><i>Sustineant vel aspera</i></l>
    <l><i>Tenerrimos offendant:</i></l>
    <l><i>De preciosis pellibus</i></l>
  <p cont="true"><i>Subtilibus &amp; mollibus</i><br /><i>Camisias emendant.</i><br /><i>Ut placeant hominibus</i><br /><i>Nituntur suis crinibus</i><br /><i>Incedere politis:</i><br /><i>Coronas in capitibus</i><br /><i>Ferunt, de pilis mitibus,</i><br /><i>Et rebus exquisitis.</i><br /><i>Sic imitantur Dominum,</i><br /><i>Qui pro salute hominum</i><br /><i>Est spinis coronatus:</i><br /><i>Sic serviunt altissimo</i><br /><i>Qui non pepercit Filio,</i><br /><i>Dum stetit immolatus.</i><br /><i>In cruce nudis genibus,</i><br /><i>Et manibus &amp; pedibus</i><br /><i>Et dextra perforatus.</i><br /><i>Sic deridetur Dominus,</i><br /><i>A Servo nihilominus</i><br /><i>In via prosperatus.</i><br /><i>Præbendas habet quatuor,</i><br /><i>Et est Ecclesiæ pastor,</i><br /><i>Vel potius mercator:</i><br /><i>Si forte chorum visitat,</i><br /><i>Non propter Jesum ibi stat,</i></p>
    <p type="foot">Collegiorum jocus,</p>
  </main_text><notes>The right column is set beside the left and its lines are read after the left column; the first lines of the right column are the continuation of the same verse. Parts of the page toward the bottom of the left column are cut off in this part and continue on the next part. The line "Collegiorum jocus," at left is a marginal side-line, transcribed as a foot note. Parts of the scan are faint or stained; words were read with care but some verse endings may be imperfect.</notes></page>
